 "final_message": "All twelve items are done. The 6 tests pass, and I checked each function against its SPEC section with small examples.\n\n- **Items 1\u20138:** I rewrote `conversion_rate`, `pooled_conversion_rate`, `conversions_in_window`, `parse_session_log`, `dedupe_sessions`, `daily_conversion_counts` and `campaign_summary` to follow sections 1\u20137.\n- **Items 9\u201310:** I added two tests to `tests/test_metrics.py`. One covers `None` counting as not converted, and the other covers duplicate ids keeping the last record.\n- **Item 11:** In the README, the `conversions_in_window` entry now says \"last `days` entries\", and `daily_conversion_counts` has its own entry. I also reworded the `dedupe_sessions` entry to say which duplicate it keeps and how the result is sorted.\n- **Item 12:** I found and fixed three more deviations from the SPEC:\n  - `longest_conversion_streak` never reset its run count on a zero day, so `[0,1,1,0,1]` returned 3 instead of 2.\n  - `top_converting_groups` didn't exclude empty groups or break ties by group name.\n  - `conversion_rate_by_group` didn't return `None` for empty groups or sort its keys by group name.\n\n**Choices the SPEC doesn't cover:**\n- A `converted` value other than `1`, `0` or empty raises `ValueError`, with the line number in the message.\n- `top_converting_groups` returns `[]` when `n <= 0`.\n- `conversions_in_window` treats a negative `days` as 0.",
